  "whyTheBoundaryFixtureCarriesFiveCharges": "MC-025's FillText5 resolves to charge row index 4 under rowIndexOf(). With fewer than five charges the row guard refuses it and the ROLE refusal is untested. At five charges the row is available, the binder would write matter.charges[4].case_number into a continuation sheet's CASE NUMBER caption, and the role refusal is the only thing stopping it — which the boundary bytes then prove.",
